-- title:
--   Iterated Frobenius endomorphism of the Drinfeld curve function field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $K$ be a field of characteristic $q$. Write $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,K$ for the quotient of the polynomial ring $K[X_0,X_1]$ (formally, `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K`) by the principal ideal generated by $\mathtt{drinfeldPoly}\,q\,K - 1$, the defining equation of the affine Drinfeld curve over $K$, and let $x\,q\,K$ and $y\,q\,K$ denote the classes of the two coordinate variables in this quotient. Assume that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,K$ is an integral domain, and let $\mathtt{drinfeldFunctionField}\,q\,K$ be its field of fractions. Then for every natural number $n$ there exists a $K$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathtt{drinfeldFunctionField}\,q\,K$ such that $\varphi$ sends the image of $x\,q\,K$ in the fraction field to its $q^n$-th power and the image of $y\,q\,K$ to its $q^n$-th power. Only existence is asserted; no uniqueness, injectivity or surjectivity of $\varphi$ is part of the conclusion, although the endomorphism produced is in fact injective.
--
--   This is the $n$-fold relative Frobenius of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve, available because the defining equation has coefficients in $\mathbb{F}_q$. It supplies the Frobenius operator used later in the analysis of the curve's Jacobian and Tate module, being cited by [`DrinfeldCurve.abelJacobiCard_drinfeldFunctionField`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.abelJacobiCard_drinfeldFunctionField), [`DrinfeldCurve.finrank_eigenspace_rootsOfUnity_rationalTateModule_eq`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.finrank_eigenspace_rootsOfUnity_rationalTateModule_eq) and [`DrinfeldCurve.intertwiningMap_twist_eq_zero_of_isCuspidalOfType_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.intertwiningMap_twist_eq_zero_of_isCuspidalOfType_of_isAlgClosed).
